s B, C, and D are incorrect and may be the result of errors when applying the distributive property.</p><p><!--EndFragment--></p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959629,"updateDate":1691007959629}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959629, 1691007959629),
    ($SATQ$630897df$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$09153-DC$SATQ$, $SATQ$disclosed$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Advanced Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$P$SATQ$, $SATQ$P.B.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Nonlinear equations in one variable and systems of equations in two variables $SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 4, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p class="stem_paragraph ">The speed of sound in dry air, <span class="italic"><span class="formatted_text font_style:italic ">v</span></span>, can be modeled by the formula <span class="math_expression "><span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/630897df/img_004_63b63bfa.png" alt="v equals, 331 point 3 plus 0 point 6 0 6 times T"></span></span>, where <span class="italic">T</span> is the temperature in degrees Celsius and <span class="italic">v</span> is measured in meters per&nbsp;second. Which of the following correctly expresses <span class="italic">T</span> in terms&nbsp;of&nbsp;<span class="italic">v</span>&nbsp;?</p>
$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"a","content":"<span class=\"math_expression \">\n            <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/630897df/img_000_b4bdafe0.png\" alt=\"T equals, the fraction with numerator, v plus 0 point 6 0 6, and denominator, 331 point 3\"></span></span>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<span class=\"math_expression \">\n            <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/630897df/img_001_c781896f.png\" alt=\"T equals, the fraction with numerator, v minus 0 point 6 0 6, and denominator, 331 point 3\"></span></span>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<span class=\"math_expression \">\n            <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/630897df/img_002_4e9c5094.png\" alt=\"T equals, the fraction with numerator, v plus 331 point 3, and denominator, 0 point 6 0 6\"></span></span>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<span class=\"math_expression \">\n            <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/630897df/img_003_61c99362.png\" alt=\"T equals, the fraction with numerator, v minus 331 point 3, and denominator, 0 point 6 0 6\"></span></span>\n"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Choice D is correct. To express <span class="italic">T</span> in terms of <span class="italic">v</span>, subtract 331.3 from both sides of the equation, which gives <span class="italic">v</span> &ndash; 331.3 = 0.606<span class="italic">T</span>. Dividing both sides of the equation by 0.606 gives <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/630897df/img_005_5fc9989e.png" alt="the fraction with numerator v minus 331 point 3, and denominator 0 point 6 0 6, equals T"></span>.<p>Choices A, B, and C are incorrect and are the result of incorrect steps while solving for <span class="italic">T</span>.</p></p>
$SATQ$, false, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$Multiple Choice$SATQ$, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ${"questionId":"630897df","external_id":null,"disclosed_item_id":"09153-DC","source":"disclosed","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"P","domain":"Advanced Math","skill_cd":"P.B.","skill_desc":"Nonlinear equations in one variable and systems of equations in two variables ","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":4,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">The speed of sound in dry air, <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"formatted_text font_style:italic \">v</span></span>, can be modeled by the formula <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/630897df/img_004_63b63bfa.png\" alt=\"v equals, 331 point 3 plus 0 point 6 0 6 times T\"></span></span>, where <span class=\"italic\">T</span> is the temperature in degrees Celsius and <span class=\"italic\">v</span> is measured in meters per&nbsp;second. Which of the following correctly expresses <span class=\"italic\">T</span> in terms&nbsp;of&nbsp;<span class=\"italic\">v</span>&nbsp;?</p>\n","answerOptions":[{"id":"a","content":"<span class=\"math_expression \">\n            <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/630897df/img_000_b4bdafe0.png\" alt=\"T equals, the fraction with numerator, v plus 0 point 6 0 6, and denominator, 331 point 3\"></span></span>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<span class=\"math_expression \">\n            <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/630897df/img_001_c781896f.png\" alt=\"T equals, the fraction with numerator, v minus