quals, the fraction with numerator, v minus 331 point 3, and denominator, 0 point 6 0 6\"></span></span>\n"}},"correct_choice":"d","rationale":"<p>Choice D is correct. To express <span class=\"italic\">T</span> in terms of <span class=\"italic\">v</span>, subtract 331.3 from both sides of the equation, which gives <span class=\"italic\">v</span> &ndash; 331.3 = 0.606<span class=\"italic\">T</span>. Dividing both sides of the equation by 0.606 gives <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"the fraction with numerator v minus 331 point 3, and denominator 0 point 6 0 6, equals T\"></span>.<p>Choices A, B, and C are incorrect and are the result of incorrect steps while solving for <span class=\"italic\">T</span>.</p></p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959636,"updateDate":1691007959636}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959636, 1691007959636),
    ($SATQ$635f54ee$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$05720-DC$SATQ$, $SATQ$disclosed$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Advanced Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$P$SATQ$, $SATQ$P.C.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Nonlinear functions$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 7, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p class="stem_paragraph ">The surface area of a cube is <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/635f54ee/img_004_baf3c8df.png" alt="6 times, open parenthesis, the fraction a, over 4, close parenthesis, squared"></span>, where <span class="italic">a</span> is a positive constant. Which of the following gives the perimeter of one face of the&nbsp;cube?</p>
$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"a","content":"<p><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/635f54ee/img_000_c98e53ce.png\" alt=\"the fraction a, over 4\"></span></p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/635f54ee/img_001_6253433b.png\" alt=\"a\"></span></p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/635f54ee/img_002_87833ed2.png\" alt=\"4 a\"></span></p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/635f54ee/img_003_fb1f5765.png\" alt=\"6 a\"></span></p>\n"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Choice B is correct. A cube has 6 faces of equal area, so if the total surface area of a cube is <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/635f54ee/img_005_baf3c8df.png" alt="6 times, open parenthesis, a, over 4, close parenthesis, squared"></span>, then the area of one face is <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/635f54ee/img_006_1ae0ab32.png" alt="open parenthesis, a, over 4, close parenthesis, squared"></span>. Likewise, the area of one face of a cube is the square of one of its edges; therefore, if the area of one face is <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/635f54ee/img_007_1ae0ab32.png" alt="open parenthesis, a, over 4, close parenthesis, squared"></span>, then the length of one edge of the cube is <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/635f54ee/img_008_c98e53ce.png" alt="a, over 4"></span>. Since the perimeter of one face of a cube is four times the length of one edge, the perimeter is <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/635f54ee/img_009_020185f0.png" alt="4 times the fraction a, over 4, equals a"></span>.<br>Choice A is incorrect because if the perimeter of one face of the cube is <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/635f54ee/img_010_c98e53ce.png" alt="a, over 4"></span>, then the total surface area of the cube is <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/635f54ee/img_011_2d2e9cce.png" alt="6 times, open parenthesis, the fraction with numerator a, over 4, and denominator 4, close parenthesis, squared, equals, 6 times, open parenthesis, a, over 16, close parenthesis, squared"></span>, which is not <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/635f54ee/img_012_baf3c8df.png" alt="6 times, open parenthesis, a, over 4, close parenthesis, squared"></span>. Choice C is incorrect because if the perimeter of one face of the cube is 4<span class="italic">a</span>, then the total surface area of the cube is <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/635f54ee/img_013_4c757571.png" alt="6 times, open parenthesis, the fraction 4 a, over 4, close parenthesis, squared, equals 6 a, squared"></span>, which is not <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/635f54ee/img_014_baf3c8df.png" alt="6 times, open parenthesis, a, over 4, close parenthesis, squared"></span>. Choice D is incorrect because if the perimeter of one face of the cube is 6<span class="italic">a</span>, then the total surface area of the cube is <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/635f54ee/img_015_f20e5683.png" alt="6 times, open parenthesis, the fraction 6 a, over 4, close parenthesis, squared, equals, 6 times, open parenthesis, the fraction 3 a, over 2, close parenthesis, squared"></span>, which is not <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/635f54ee/img_016_baf3c8df.png" alt="6 times, open parenthesis, a, over 4, close parenthesis, squared"></span>.</p>
