th-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/652054da/img_006_468d73a8.png" alt="three halves"></span> will isolate <span class="italic">p</span>. This yields <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/652054da/img_007_b1ff28fc.png" alt="two thirds s equals, two thirds times, three halves p"></span>, which simplifies to <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/652054da/img_008_4dacce3e.png" alt="two thirds s, equals p"></span>. Therefore, <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/652054da/img_009_552f85e1.png" alt="p equals, two thirds s"></span>.<p>Choices B, C, and D are incorrect and may result from errors made when rearranging the equation to solve for <span class="italic">p</span>.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>
