$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p class="stem_paragraph ">An engineer wanted to identify the best angle for a cooling fan in an engine in order to get the greatest airflow. The engineer discovered that the function above models the airflow <span class="math_expression "><span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6676f055/img_001_efc8e0ee.png" alt="f of theta"></span></span>, in cubic feet per minute, as a function of the angle of the fan <span class="italic"><span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6676f055/img_002_2703d96e.png" alt="theta"></span></span>, in degrees. According to the model, what angle, in degrees, gives the greatest airflow?</p>
$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"a","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">&ndash;0.28</p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">0.28</p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">27</p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \">880</p>\n"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Choice C is correct. The function&nbsp;<span class="italic">f</span>&nbsp;is quadratic, so it will have either a maximum or a minimum at the vertex of the graph. Since the coefficient of the quadratic term&nbsp;(&ndash;0.28)&nbsp;is negative, the vertex will be at a maximum. The equation <span class="italic">f</span>(<span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6676f055/img_003_2703d96e.png" alt="theta"></span>) = &ndash;0.28(<span class="italic"><span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6676f055/img_004_2703d96e.png" alt="theta"></span></span> &ndash; 27)<sup>2</sup> + 880 is given in vertex form, so the vertex is at&nbsp;<span class="italic"><span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6676f055/img_005_2703d96e.png" alt="theta"></span></span> = 27. Therefore,&nbsp;an angle of 27 degrees&nbsp;gives the greatest airflow.<p>Choices A and B are&nbsp;incorrect and may be the result of&nbsp;misidentifying&nbsp;which value in a quadratic equation in vertex form represents the vertex.&nbsp;Choice D is incorrect.&nbsp;This choice identifies the maximum value of <span class="italic">f</span>(<span class="italic"><span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6676f055/img_006_2703d96e.png" alt="theta"></span></span>) rather than the value of&nbsp;<span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6676f055/img_007_2703d96e.png" alt="theta"></span> for which <span class="italic">f</span>(<span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6676f055/img_008_2703d96e.png" alt="theta"></span>) is maximized.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>
