	<mi>w</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>14</mn>
</mrow>
</math>, it follows that&nbsp;<math alttext="f left parenthesis 14 right parenthesis equals 1,176"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mn>14</mn></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1,176</mn></math> means that <math alttext="f left parenthesis w right parenthesis"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>w</mi></mfenced></math> is&nbsp;<math alttext="1,176"><mn>1,176</mn></math> if <math alttext="w equals 14"><mrow>
	<mi>w</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>14</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. In the given context, this means that if the width of the rectangle is <math alttext="14 ft"><mn>14</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mtext>ft</mtext></math>, then the area of the rectangle is <math alttext="1,176 ft squared"><mn>1,176</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mtext>ft</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>
