t-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect and may result from interpreting <math alttext=\"f left parenthesis w right parenthesis\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>w</mi></mfenced></math> as the width, in <math alttext=\"ft\"><mtext>ft</mtext></math>, of the rectangle if its area is <math alttext=\"w ft squared\"><mi>w</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mtext>ft</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, rather than as the area, in <math alttext=\"ft Superscript 2\"><msup><mtext>ft</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, of the rectangle if its width is <math alttext=\"w ft\"><mi>w</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mtext>ft</mtext></math>.</p>","origin":"manifold","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The function <math alttext=\"f left parenthesis w right parenthesis equals 6 w squared\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>w</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow><msup><mi>w</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> gives the area of a rectangle, <math alttext=\"in square feet left parenthesis ft squared right parenthesis\"><mtext>in</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>square</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>feet</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><msup><mtext>ft</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></mfenced></math>, if its width is <math alttext=\"w ft\"><mi>w</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>ft</mtext></math> and its length is <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math> times its width. Which of the following is the best interpretation of <math alttext=\"f left parenthesis 14 right parenthesis equals 1,176\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>14</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1,176</mn>\n</math>?</p>","externalid":"969792b2-4ab7-4fe4-8d9e-e1a709101015","templateid":"940ce423-11f4-4f23-81ee-dbb0b758ef99","vaultid":"da7a966c-bd02-4bdd-ae64-af5fcab66004","type":"mcq","answerOptions":[{"id":"6a44f3f6-0bba-46a8-9507-a5b79c54d226","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">If the width of the rectangle is <math alttext=\"14 ft\"><mrow><mn>14</mn></mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>ft</mtext></math>, then the area of the rectangle is <math alttext=\"1,176 ft squared\"><mrow><mn>1,176</mn></mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mtext>ft</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></math>.</p>"},{"id":"603e8a84-c993-4dc1-b31a-470f9bfab2ae","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">If the width of the rectangle is <math alttext=\"14 ft\"><mrow><mn>14</mn></mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>ft</mtext></math>, then the length of the rectangle is <math alttext=\"1,176 ft\"><mrow><mn>1,176</mn></mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>ft</mtext></math>.</p>"},{"id":"a4fc4b97-17da-4231-b9c3-b7cc474672ec","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">If the width of the rectangle is <math alttext=\"1,176 ft\"><mrow><mn>1,176</mn></mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>ft</mtext></math>, then the length of the rectangle is <math alttext=\"14 ft\"><mrow><mn>14</mn></mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>ft</mtext></math>.</p>"},{"id":"10619f28-29e5-4722-a1d1-9f519439c749","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">If the width of the rectangle is <math alttext=\"1,176 ft\"><mrow><mn>1,176</mn></mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>ft</mtext></math>, then the area of the rectangle is <math alttext=\"14 ft squared\"><mrow><mn>14</mn></mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mtext>ft</mtext><mn>2</mn></msup></math>.</p>"}],"correct_answer":["A"]},"createDate":1691007959825,"updateDate":1691007959825}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959825, 1691007959825),
    ($SATQ$68607eca$SATQ$, $SATQ$ca334282-00d9-4e64-9f61-edc6bc5d7646$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Advanced Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$P$SATQ$, $SATQ$P.C.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Nonlinear functions$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 5, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">On April <math alttext="1"><mn>1</mn></math>, there were <math alttext="233"><mn>233</mn></math> views of an advertisement posted on a website. Every <math alttext="2"><mn>2</mn></math> days after April <math alttext="1"><mn>1</mn></math>, the number of views of the advertisement had increased by <math alttext="70 percent sign"><mn>70</mn>
<mo>%</mo></math> of the number of views&nbsp;<math alttext="2"><mn>2</mn></math> days earlier. The function <math alttext="f"><mi>f</mi></math> gives the predicted number of views <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> days after April <math alttext="1"><mn>1</mn></math>. Which equation defines <math alttext="f"><mi>f</mi></math>?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"1052d6ab-4491-47e2-a58b-b3877d48f351","content":"<p><math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 233 left parenthesis 0.70 right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction x Over 2 EndFraction\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>233</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>0.70</mn></mfenced><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></math></p>"},{"id":"0faf734d-17de-4d34-b391-42e8c7f78a51","content":"<p><math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 233 left parenthesis 0.70 right parenthesis Superscript 2 x\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>233</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>0.70</mn></mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup></math></p>"},{"id":"4eb392b1-fec1-480f-a299-03f891e06132","content":"<p><math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 233 left parenthesis 1.70 right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction x Over 2 EndFraction\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>233</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>1.70</mn></mfenced><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></math></p>"},{"id":"657efc74-adb4-46b2-a50b-f97d00d87a2e","content":"<p><math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 233 left parenthesis 1.70 right parenthesis Superscript 2 x\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>233</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>1.70</mn></mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup></math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["4eb392b1-fec1-480f-a299-03f891e06132"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is correct. It&rsquo;s given that on April <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="1"><mn>1</mn></math>, there were <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="233"><mn>233</mn></math> views of the advertisement. It&rsquo;s also given that every <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="2"><mn>2</mn></math> days after April <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="1"><mn>1</mn></math>, the number of views of the advertisement had increased by <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="70 percent sign"><mn>70</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of the number of views <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="2"><mn>2</mn></math> days earlier. This situation can be represented by an exponential function of the form <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals a left parenthesis 1 plus StartFraction r Over 100 EndFraction right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction x Over c EndFraction"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>r</mi><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mi>c</mi></mfrac></msup></math>, where <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="a"><mi>a</mi></math> is the number of views on April <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="1"><mn>1</mn></math> and every <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="c"><mi>c</mi></math> days after April <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="1"><mn>1</mn></math>, the number of views had increased by <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="r percent sign"><mi>r</mi><mo>%</mo></math> of the number of views <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="c"><mi>c</mi></math> days earlier. It follows that <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="a equals 233"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>233</mn></math>, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="r equals 70"><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>70</mn></math>, and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="c equals 2"><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>. Substituting <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="233"><mn>233</mn></math> for <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="a"><mi>a</mi></math>, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="70"><mn>70</mn></math> for <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="r"><mi>r</mi></math>, and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="2"><mn>2</mn></math> for <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="c"><mi>c</mi></math> in the equation <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals a left parenthesis 1 plus StartFraction r Over 100 EndFraction right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction x Over c EndFraction"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>r</mi><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mi>c</mi></mfrac></msup></math> yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 233 left parenthesis 1 plus StartFraction 70 Over 100 EndFraction right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction x Over 2 EndFraction"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>233</mn><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>70</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></math>, or <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 233 left parenthesis 1.70 right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction x Over 2 EndFraction"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>233</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>1.70</mn></mfenced><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect. This function gives the predicted number of views for an advertisement for which every <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="2"><mn>2</mn></math> days, the number of views was <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="70 percent sign"><mn>70</mn><mo>%</mo></math>, rather than&nbsp;increased by <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="70 percent sign"><mn>70</mn><mo>%</mo></math>, of the number of views <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="2"><mn>2</mn></math> days earlier.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect. This function gives the predicted number of views for an advertisement for which every <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="one half"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> days, the number of views was <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="70 percent sign"><mn>70</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of the number of views <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="one half"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> days earlier, rather than an advertisement for which every <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="2"><mn>2</mn></math> days, the number of views had increased by <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="70 percent sign"><mn>70</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of the number of views <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="2"><mn>2</mn></math> days earlier.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect. This function gives the predicted number of views for an advertisement for which every <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="one half"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> days, rather than every <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="2"><mn>2</mn></math> days, the number of views had increased by <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="70 percent sign"><mn>70</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of the number of views <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="one half"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> days earlier, rather than <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="2"><mn>2</mn></math> days earlier.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"68607eca","external_id":"ca334282-00d9-4e64-9f61-edc6bc5d7646","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"60c3ffa2-08a6-4d34-a40a-3701d00ea104","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"P","domain":"Advanced Math","skill_cd":"P.C.","skill_desc":"Nonlinear functions","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":5,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">On April <math alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn></math>, there were <math alttext=\"233\"><mn>233</mn></math> views of an advertisement posted on a website. Every <math alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn></math> days after April <math alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn></math>, the number of views of the advertisement had increased by <math alttext=\"70 percent sign\"><mn>70</mn>\n<mo>%</mo></math> of the number of views&nbsp;<math alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn></math> days earlier. The function <math alttext=\"f\"><mi>f</mi></math> gives the predicted number of views <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> days after April <math alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn></math>. Which equation defines <math alttext=\"f\"><mi>f</mi></math>?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"105