umber of views of the advertisement had increased by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"70 percent sign\"><mn>70</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of the number of views <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn></math> days earlier. This situation can be represented by an exponential function of the form <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals a left parenthesis 1 plus StartFraction r Over 100 EndFraction right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction x Over c EndFraction\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>r</mi><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mi>c</mi></mfrac></msup></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi></math> is the number of views on April <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn></math> and every <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"c\"><mi>c</mi></math> days after April <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn></math>, the number of views had increased by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r percent sign\"><mi>r</mi><mo>%</mo></math> of the number of views <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"c\"><mi>c</mi></math> days earlier. It follows that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"a equals 233\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>233</mn></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r equals 70\"><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>70</mn></math>, and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"c equals 2\"><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>. Substituting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"233\"><mn>233</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"70\"><mn>70</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi></math>, and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"c\"><mi>c</mi></math> in the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals a left parenthesis 1 plus StartFraction r Over 100 EndFraction right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction x Over c EndFraction\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>r</mi><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mi>c</mi></mfrac></msup></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 233 left parenthesis 1 plus StartFraction 70 Over 100 EndFraction right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction x Over 2 EndFraction\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>233</mn><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>70</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 233 left parenthesis 1.70 right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction x Over 2 EndFraction\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>233</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>1.70</mn></mfenced><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect. This function gives the predicted number of views for an advertisement for which every <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn></math> days, the number of views was <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"70 percent sign\"><mn>70</mn><mo>%</mo></math>, rather than&nbsp;increased by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"70 percent sign\"><mn>70</mn><mo>%</mo></math>, of the number of views <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn></math> days earlier.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect. This function gives the predicted number of views for an advertisement for which every <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"one half\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> days, the number of views was <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"70 percent sign\"><mn>70</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of the number of views <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"one half\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> days earlier, rather than an advertisement for which every <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn></math> days, the number of views had increased by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"70 percent sign\"><mn>70</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of the number of views <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn></math> days earlier.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect. This function gives the predicted number of views for an advertisement for which every <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"one half\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> days, rather than every <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn></math> days, the number of views had increased by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"70 percent sign\"><mn>70</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of the number of views <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"one half\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> days earlier, rather than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn></math> days earlier.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1755117017724,"pPcc":"SAT#P","questionId":"68607eca","skill_cd":"P.C.","score_band_range_cd":5,"skill_desc":"Nonlinear functions","createDate":1755117017724,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Advanced Math","ibn":"","external_id":"ca334282-00d9-4e64-9f61-edc6bc5d7646","primary_class_cd":"P","uId":"60c3ffa2-08a6-4d34-a40a-3701d00ea104","difficulty":"M"},"raw_detail":{"type":"mcq","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">On April <math alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn></math>, there were <math alttext=\"233\"><mn>233</mn></math> views of an advertisement posted on a website. Every <math alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn></math> days after April <math alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn></math>, the number of views of the advertisement had increased by <math alttext=\"70 percent sign\"><mn>70</mn>\n<mo>%</mo></math> of the number of views&nbsp;<math alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn></math> days earlier. The function <math alttext=\"f\"><mi>f</mi></math> gives the predicted number of views <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> days after April <math alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn></math>. Which equation defines <math alttext=\"f\"><mi>f</mi></math>?</p>","keys":["4eb392b1-fec1-480f-a299-03f891e06132"],"answerOptions":[{"id":"1052d6ab-4491-47e2-a58b-b3877d48f351","content":"<p><math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 233 left parenthesis 0.70 right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction x Over 2 EndFraction\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>233</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>0.70</mn></mfenced><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></math></p>"},{"id":"0faf734d-17de-4d34-b391-42e8c7f78a51","content":"<p><math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 233 left parenthesis 0.70 right parenthesis Superscript 2 x\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>233</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>0.70</mn></mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup></math></p>"},{"id":"4eb392b1-fec1-480f-a299-03f891e06132","content":"<p><math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 233 left parenthesis 1.70 right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction x Over 2 EndFraction\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>233</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>1.70</mn></mfenced><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></math></p>"},{"id":"657efc74-adb4-46b2-a50b-f97d00d87a2e","content":"<p><math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 233 left parenthesis 1.70 right parenthesis Superscript 2 x\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>233</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>1.70</mn></mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup></math></p>"}],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is correct. It&rsquo;s given that on April <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn></math>, there were <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"233\"><mn>233</mn></math> views of the advertisement. It&rsquo;s also given that every <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn></math> days after April <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn></math>, the number of views of the advertisement had increased by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"70 percent sign\"><mn>70</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of the number of views <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn></math> days earlier. This situation can be represented by an exponential function of the form <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals a left parenthesis 1 plus StartFraction r Over 100 EndFraction right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction x Over c EndFraction\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>r</mi><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mi>c</mi></mfrac></msup></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi></math> is the number of views on April <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn></math> and every <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"c\"><mi>c</mi></math> days after April <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn></math>, the number of views had increased by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r percent sign\"><mi>r</mi><mo>%</mo></math> of the number of views <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"c\"><mi>c</mi></math> days earlier. It follows that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"a equals 233\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>233</mn></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r equals 70\"><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>70</mn></math>, and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"c equals 2\"><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math>. Substituting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"233\"><mn>233</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"70\"><mn>70</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"r\"><mi>r</mi></math>, and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn></math> for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"c\"><mi>c</mi></math> in the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals a left parenthesis 1 plus StartFraction r Over 100 EndFraction right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction x Over c EndFraction\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>r</mi><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mi>c</mi></mfrac></msup></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 233 left parenthesis 1 plus StartFraction 70 Over 100 EndFraction right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction x Over 2 EndFraction\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>233</mn><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>70</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 233 left parenthesis 1.70 right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction x Over 2 EndFraction\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>233</mn><msup><mfenced><mn>1.70</mn></mfenced><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect. This function gives the predicted number of views for an advertisement for which every <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn></math> days, the number of views was <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"70 percent sign\"><mn>70</mn><mo>%</mo></math>, rather than&nbsp;increased by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"70 percent sign\"><mn>70</mn><mo>%</mo></math>, of the number of views <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn></math> days earlier.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect. This function gives the predicted number of views for an advertisement for which every <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"one half\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> days, the number of views was <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"70 percent sign\"><mn>70</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of the number of views <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"one half\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> days earlier, rather than an advertisement for which every <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn></math> days, the number of views had increased by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"70 percent sign\"><mn>70</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of the number of views <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn></math> days earlier.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect. This function gives the predicted number of views for an advertisement for which every <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"one half\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> days, rather than every <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn></math> days, the number of views had increased by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"70 percent sign\"><mn>70</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of the number of views <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"one half\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> days earlier, rather than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn></math> days earlier.</p>","externalid":"ca334282-00d9-4e64-9f61-edc6bc5d7646","correct_answer":["C"]},"createDate":1755117017724,"updateDate":1755117017724}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1755117017724, 1755117017724),
