<div role="region" aria-label="Long description for graph of a curve" class="sr-only"><ul>
<li>Moving from left to right:
<ul>
<li>The curve passes from quadrant 3 to quadrant 4.</li>
<li>In quadrant 3, the curve trends up sharply to point (0 comma negative 5).</li>
<li>In quadrant 4, the curve trends up gradually.</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>As x increases, the curve approaches the line y equals negative 4.</li>
<li>The curve passes through the following points:
<ul>
<li>(negative 1 comma negative 9)</li>
<li>(0 comma negative 5)</li>
<li>(1 comma negative 4.2)</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul></div></figure></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">What is the <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math>-intercept of the graph shown?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"df1e4f8e-387e-4276-be0d-5dbe9a9cf973","content":"<p><math alttext=\"left parenthesis negative 1 comma negative 9 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mrow></mfenced></math></p>"},{"id":"0e8dba99-9114-4a9f-8382-0f97b0bd631e","content":"<p><math alttext=\"left parenthesis 0 comma negative 5 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mrow></mfenced></math></p>"},{"id":"f98b3f37-8a95-4690-b3fd-a2220b83bc76","content":"<p><math alttext=\"left parenthesis 0 comma negative 4 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow></mfenced></math></p>"},{"id":"8a487fd9-fcb6-47f8-81a6-cb2748f5866b","content":"<p><math alttext=\"left parenthesis 0 comma 0 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["0e8dba99-9114-4a9f-8382-0f97b0bd631e"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is correct. The <em>y</em>-intercept of a graph in the <em>xy</em>-plane is the point&nbsp;<math alttext="left parenthesis x comma y right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> on the graph where <math alttext="x equals 0"><mrow>
	<mi>x</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>0</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. At <math alttext="x equals 0"><mrow>
	<mi>x</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>0</mn>
</mrow>
</math>, the corresponding value of <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math> is <math alttext="negative 5"><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn>
</math>. Therefore, the <em>y</em>-intercept of the graph shown&nbsp;is <math alttext="left parenthesis 0 comma negative 5 right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>
<p>Choice C is incorrect. This is the <em>y</em>-intercept of a graph in the <em>xy</em>-plane that intersects the <em>y</em>-axis at <math alttext="y equals negative 4"><mrow>
	<mi>y</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn>
</mrow>
</math>, not <math alttext="y equals negative 5"><mrow>
	<mi>y</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn>
</mrow>
</math>.</p>
<p>Choice D is incorrect. This is the <em>y</em>-intercept of a graph in the <em>xy</em>-plane that intersects the <em>y</em>-axis at <math alttext="y equals 0"><mrow>
	<mi>y</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>0</mn>
</mrow>
</math>, not <math alttext="y equals negative 5"><mrow>
	<mi>y</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn>
</mrow>
