quals x"><mi>b</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>72</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></math>, or <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x equals b y minus 72 y"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>72</mn><mi>y</mi></math>. Therefore, the equation <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x equals b y minus 72 y"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>72</mn><mi>y</mi></math> correctly expresses <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x"><mi>x</mi></math> in terms of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="b"><mi>b</mi></math> and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y"><mi>y</mi></math>.</p>
<p>Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p>Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
