1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi></math> in terms of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi></math>.</p>\n<p>Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p>Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p>Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>","externalid":"7b75e7d1-53d8-4028-84e1-be077af6c888","correct_answer":["D"]},"createDate":1755117017719,"updateDate":1755117017719}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1755117017719, 1755117017719),
    ($SATQ$6aefc52b$SATQ$, $SATQ$c7ec775c-6d72-46ae-8501-bb2d64052015$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Advanced Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$P$SATQ$, $SATQ$P.B.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Nonlinear equations in one variable and systems of equations in two variables $SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 7, $SATQ$spr$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: center;"><math alttext="y equals negative 2.5"><mrow>
