t, and denominator 4\"></span>. Dividing 2 from both the numerator and denominator yields <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6ce95fc8/img_016_a4ebd312.png\" alt=\"the fraction with numerator 1 plus the square root of 11, end root, and denominator 2\"></span> or <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6ce95fc8/img_017_b16458d9.png\" alt=\"the fraction with numerator 1 minus the square root of 11, end root, and denominator 2\"></span>. Of these two solutions, only <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6ce95fc8/img_018_a4ebd312.png\" alt=\"the fraction with numerator 1 plus the square root of 11, end root, and denominator 2\"></span> is present among the choices. Thus, the correct choice is D.<p>Choice A is incorrect and may result from a computational or conceptual error. Choice B is incorrect and may result from using <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6ce95fc8/img_019_02fcd523.png\" alt=\"x equals, the fraction with numerator negative b plus or minus the square root of b squared, minus 4 a c, end root, and denominator a, end fraction \"></span> instead of <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6ce95fc8/img_020_3c23ebed.png\" alt=\"x equals, the fraction with numerator negative b, plus or minus the square root of b squared, minus 4 a c, end root, and denominator 2 a, end fraction \"></span> as the quadratic formula. Choice C is incorrect and may result from rewriting <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6ce95fc8/img_021_9119edcf.png\" alt=\"the square root of 44 \"></span> as <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6ce95fc8/img_022_8d64c9e3.png\" alt=\"4 times the square root of 11\"></span> instead of <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/6ce95fc8/img_023_1628fe78.png\" alt=\"2 times the square root of 11\"></span>.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n","answer_style":"Multiple Choice","section":"Math","image_count":24,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959615,"pPcc":"SAT#P","questionId":"6ce95fc8","skill_cd":"P.B.","score_band_range_cd":7,"skill_desc":"Nonlinear equations in one variable and systems of equations in two variables ","createDate":1691007959615,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Advanced Math","ibn":"016807-DC","external_id":null,"primary_class_cd":"P","uId":"29704632-c2c2-4050-931d-e4d9d6376e7e","difficulty":"H"},"raw_detail":{"item_id":"016807-DC","section":"Math","body":"<div class=\"stimulus_reference \" xmlns=\"http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/apip/apipv1p0/qtiitem/imsqti_v2p1\"><p class=\"standalone_statement style:1 \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"2 x squared, minus 2, equals 2 x plus 3\"></span></span></p></div>\n","prompt":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">Which of the following is a solution to the equation above?</p>\n","answer":{"style":"Multiple Choice","choices":{"a":{"body":"<p>2</p>\n"},"b":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math-container\"><