<mn>31</mn>
<mn>3</mn>
</mfrac>
</math>. Subtracting <math alttext="5 left parenthesis x plus 7 right parenthesis"><mn>5</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;from each side of the given equation yields <math alttext="0 equals 15 left parenthesis x minus 17 right parenthesis left parenthesis x plus 7 right parenthesis minus 5 left parenthesis x plus 7 right parenthesis"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>15</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>17</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. Since <math alttext="5 left parenthesis x plus 7 right parenthesis"><mn>5</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is a common factor of each of the terms on the right-hand side of this equation, it can be rewritten as <math alttext="0 equals 5 left parenthesis x plus 7 right parenthesis left parenthesis 3 left parenthesis x minus 17 right parenthesis minus 1 right parenthesis"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>17</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. This is equivalent to <math alttext="0 equals 5 left parenthesis x plus 7 right parenthesis left parenthesis 3 x minus 51 minus 1 right parenthesis"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>51</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, or <math alttext="0 equals 5 left parenthesis x plus 7 right parenthesis left parenthesis 3 x minus 52 right parenthesis"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>52</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. Dividing both sides of this equation by <math alttext="5"><mn>5</mn>
</math> yields <math alttext="0 equals left parenthesis x plus 7 right parenthesis left parenthesis 3 x minus 52 right parenthesis"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>52</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. Since a product of two factors is equal to <math alttext="0"><mn>0</mn>
</math> if and only if at least one of the factors is <math alttext="0"><mn>0</mn>
</math>, either <math alttext="x plus 7 equals 0"><mrow>
<mrow>
<mi>x</mi>
<mo>+</mo>
<mn>7</mn>
</mrow>
<mo>=</mo>
<mn>0</mn>
</mrow>
</math> or <math alttext="3 x minus 52 equals 0"><mrow>
<mrow>
<mrow>
<mn>3</mn>
<mi>x</mi>
</mrow>
<mo>-</mo>
<mn>52</mn>
</mrow>
<mo>=</mo>
<mn>0</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. Subtracting <math alttext="7"><mn>7</mn>
</math> from both sides of the equation <math alttext="x plus 7 equals 0"><mrow>
<mrow>
<mi>x</mi>
<mo>+</mo>
<mn>7</mn>
</mrow>
<mo>=</mo>
<mn>0</mn>
</mrow>
</math> yields <math alttext="x equals negative 7"><mrow>
<mi>x</mi>
<mo>=</mo>
<mrow>
<mo>-</mo>
<mn>7</mn>
</mrow>
</mrow>
</math>. Adding <math alttext="52"><mn>52</mn>
</math> to both sides of the equation <math alttext="3 x minus 52 equals 0"><mrow>
<mrow>
<mrow>
<mn>3</mn>
<mi>x</mi>
</mrow>
<mo>-</mo>
<mn>52</mn>
</mrow>
<mo>=</mo>
<mn>0</mn>
</mrow>
</math> yields <math alttext="3 x equals 52"><mrow>
