ow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. Since <math alttext=\"5 left parenthesis x plus 7 right parenthesis\"><mn>5</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is a common factor of each of the terms on the right-hand side of this equation, it can be rewritten as <math alttext=\"0 equals 5 left parenthesis x plus 7 right parenthesis left parenthesis 3 left parenthesis x minus 17 right parenthesis minus 1 right parenthesis\"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>17</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. This is equivalent to <math alttext=\"0 equals 5 left parenthesis x plus 7 right parenthesis left parenthesis 3 x minus 51 minus 1 right parenthesis\"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>51</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, or <math alttext=\"0 equals 5 left parenthesis x plus 7 right parenthesis left parenthesis 3 x minus 52 right parenthesis\"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>52</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. Dividing both sides of this equation by <math alttext=\"5\"><mn>5</mn>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"0 equals left parenthesis x plus 7 right parenthesis left parenthesis 3 x minus 52 right parenthesis\"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>52</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. Since a product of two factors is equal to <math alttext=\"0\"><mn>0</mn>\n</math> if and only if at least one of the factors is <math alttext=\"0\"><mn>0</mn>\n</math>, either <math alttext=\"x plus 7 equals 0\"><mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mi>x</mi>\n<mo>+</mo>\n<mn>7</mn>\n</mrow>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> or <math alttext=\"3 x minus 52 equals 0\"><mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mn>3</mn>\n<mi>x</mi>\n</mrow>\n<mo>-</mo>\n<mn>52</mn>\n</mrow>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Subtracting <math alttext=\"7\"><mn>7</mn>\n</math> from both sides of the equation <math alttext=\"x plus 7 equals 0\"><mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mi>x</mi>\n<mo>+</mo>\n<mn>7</mn>\n</mrow>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"x equals negative 7\"><mrow>\n<mi>x</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mrow>\n<mo>-</mo>\n<mn>7</mn>\n</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Adding <math alttext=\"52\"><mn>52</mn>\n</math> to both sides of the equation <math alttext=\"3 x minus 52 equals 0\"><mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mn>3</mn>\n<mi>x</mi>\n</mrow>\n<mo>-</mo>\n<mn>52</mn>\n</mrow>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"3 x equals 52\"><mrow>\n<mrow>\n<mn>3</mn>\n<mi>x</mi>\n</mrow>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mn>52</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Dividing both sides of this equation by <math alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"x equals StartFraction 52 Over 3 EndFraction\"><mrow>\n<mi>x</mi>\n<mo>=</mo>\n<mfrac>\n<mn>52</mn>\n<mn>3</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Therefore, the solutions to the given equation are <math alttext=\"negative 7\"><mrow>\n<mo>-</mo>\n<mn>7</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"StartFraction 52 Over 3 EndFraction\"><mfrac>\n<mn>52</mn>\n<mn>3</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</math>. It follows that the sum of the solutions to the given equation is <math alttext=\"negative 7 plus StartFraction 52 Over 3 EndFraction\"><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>52</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>, which is equivalent to <math alttext=\"negative StartFraction 21 Over 3 EndFraction plus StartFraction 52 Over 3 EndFraction\"><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>21</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>52</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>, or <math alttext=\"StartFraction 31 Over 3 EndFraction\"><mfrac>\n<mn>31</mn>\n<mn>3</mn>\n</mfrac>\n</math>. Note that 31/3 and 10.33 are examples of ways to enter a correct answer.</p>","externalid":"c442bd01-c336-457a-a300-cc899742f16e","correct_answer":["10.33","31/3"]},"createDate":1730147357395,"updateDate":1730147357395}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1730147357395, 1730147357395),
    ($SATQ$70482e20$SATQ$, $SATQ$5d93e88d-9666-4e29-baab-4dcd15423597$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$a9047e63-df4c-4f7e-93b3-730d39716027$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Advanced Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$P$SATQ$, $SATQ$P.A.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Equivalent expressions$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Which expression is equivalent to <math alttext="11 x cubed minus 5 x cubed"><mrow><mn>11</mn></mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"831050ee-a415-431c-98ee-76e5e8c5df9c","content":"<p><math alttext=\"16 x cubed\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>16</mn>\n\t<msup>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t</msup>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"f35cece2-b58c-4938-9d9a-25b5bb3b215c","content":"<p><math alttext=\"6 x cubed\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>6</mn>\n\t<msup>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t</msup>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"09555497-f9d0-4bda-80dc-62761fc4e678","content":"<p><math alttext=\"6 x Superscript 6\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>6</mn>\n\t<msup>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t<mn>6</mn>\n\t</msup>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"ca337bbe-8970-427e-a5cb-c96146b8e68f","content":"<p><math alttext=\"16 x Superscript 6\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>16</mn>\n\t<msup>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t<mn>6</mn>\n\t</msup>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["f35cece2-b58c-4938-9d9a-25b5bb3b215c"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice B is correct. The given expression can be rewritten as <math alttext="11 x cubed plus left parenthesis negative 5 right parenthesis x cubed"><mn>11</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>. Since the two terms of this expression are both constant multiples of <math alttext="x cubed"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>, they are like terms and can, therefore, be combined through addition. Adding like terms in the expression <math alttext="11 x cubed plus left parenthesis negative 5 right parenthesis x cubed"><mn>11</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math> yields <math alttext="6 x cubed"><mn>6</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>.</p>
<p>Choice A is incorrect. This is equivalent to&nbsp;<math alttext="11 x cubed plus 5 x cubed"><mn>11</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>, not&nbsp;<math alttext="11 x cubed minus 5 x cubed"><mn>11</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>.</p>
<p>Choice C is incorrect. This is equivalent to&nbsp;<math alttext="11 x Superscript 6 minus 5 x Superscript 6"><mn>11</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>6</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>6</mn></msup></math>, not&nbsp;<math alttext="11 x cubed minus 5 x cubed"><mn>11</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>.&nbsp;</p>
<p>Choice D is incorrect. This is equivalent to&nbsp;<math alttext="11 x Superscript 6 plus 5 x Superscript 6"><mn>11</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>6</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>6</mn></msup></math>, not&nbsp;<math alttext="11 x cubed minus 5 x cubed"><mn>11</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>.&nbsp;</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$manifold$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"70482e20","external_id":"5d93e88d-9666-4e29-baab-4dcd15423597","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":"a9047e63-df4c-4f7e-93b3-730d39716027","uId":"2df40af9-7dc5-4be7-b68e-8909b1b67c10","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"P","domain":"Advanced Math","skill_cd":"P.A.","skill_desc":"Equivalent expressions","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":2,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p>Which expression is equivalent to <math alttext=\"11 x cubed minus 5 x cubed\"><mrow><mn>11</mn></mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"831050ee-a415-431c-98ee-76e5e8c5df9c","content":"<p><math alttext=\"16 x cubed\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>16</mn>\n\t<msup>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t</msup>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"f35cece2-b58c-4938-9d9a-25b5bb3b215c","content":"<p><math alttext=\"6 x cubed\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>6</mn>\n\t<msup>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t</msup>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"09555497-f9d0-4bda-80dc-62761fc4e678","content":"<p><math alttext=\"6 x Superscript 6\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>6</mn>\n\t<msup>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t<mn>6</mn>\n\t</msup>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"ca337bbe-8970-427e-a5cb-c96146b8e68f","content":"<p><math alttext=\"16 x Superscript 6\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>16</mn>\n\t<msup>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t<mn>6</mn>\n\t</msup>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["f35cece2-b58c-4938-9d9a-25b5bb3b215c"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p>Choice B is correct. The given expression can be rewritten as <math alttext=\"11 x cubed plus left parenthesis negative 5 right parenthesis x cubed\"><mn>11</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>. Since the two terms of this expression are both constant multiples of <math alttext=\"x cubed\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>, they are like terms and can, therefore, be combined through addition. Adding like terms in the expression <math alttext=\"11 x cubed plus left parenthesis negative 5 right parenthesis x cubed\"><mn>11</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math> yields <math alttext=\"6 x cubed\"><mn>6</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>.</p>\n<p>Choice A is incorrect. This is equivalent to&nbsp;<math alttext=\"11 x cubed plus 5 x cubed\"><mn>11</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>, not&nbsp;<math alttext=\"11 x cubed minus 5 x cubed\"><mn>11</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>.</p>\n<p>Choice C is incorrect. This is equivalent to&nbsp;<math alttext=\"11 x Superscript 6 minus 5 x Superscript 6\"><mn>11</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>6</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>6</mn></msup></math>, not&nbsp;<math alttext=\"11 x cubed minus 5 x cubed\"><mn>11</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Choice D is incorrect. This is equivalent to&nbsp;<math alttext=\"11 x Superscript 6 plus 5 x Superscript 6\"><mn>11</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>6</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>6</mn></msup></math>, not&nbsp;<math alttext=\"11 x cubed minus 5 x cubed\"><mn>11</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>.&nbsp;</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":"manifold","position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959822,"pPcc":"SAT#P","questionId":"70482e20","skill_cd":"P.A.","score_band_range_cd":2,"skill_desc":"Equivalent expressions","createDate":1691007959822,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Advanced Math","ibn":null,"external_id":"5d93e88d-9666-4e29-baab-4dcd15423597","primary_class_cd":"P","uId":"2df40af9-7dc5-4be7-b68e-8909b1b67c10","difficulty":"E"},"raw_detail":{"keys":["f35cece2-b58c-4938-9d9a-25b5bb3b215c"],"rationale":"<p>Choice B is correct. The given expression can be rewritten as <math alttext=\"11 x cubed plus left parenthesis negative 5 right parenthesis x cubed\"><mn>11</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>. Since the two terms of this expression are both constant multiples of <math alttext=\"x cubed\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>, they are like terms and can, therefore, be combined through addition. Adding like terms in the expression <math alttext=\"11 x cubed plus left parenthesis negative 5 right parenthesis x cubed\"><mn>11</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math> yields <math alttext=\"6 x cubed\"><mn>6</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>.</p>\n<p>Choice A is incorrect. This is equivalent to&nbsp;<math alttext=\"11 x cubed plus 5 x cubed\"><mn>11</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>, not&nbsp;<math alttext=\"11 x cubed minus 5 x cubed\"><mn>11</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>.</p>\n<p>Choice C is incorrect. This is equivalent to&nbsp;<math alttext=\"11 x Superscript 6 minus 5 x Superscript 6\"><mn>11</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>6</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>6</mn></msup></math>, not&nbsp;<math alttext=\"11 x cubed minus 5 x cubed\"><mn>11</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Choice D is incorrect. This is equivalent to&nbsp;<math alttext=\"11 x Superscript 6 plus 5 x Superscript 6\"><mn>11</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>6</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>6</mn></msup></math>, not&nbsp;<math alttext=\"11 x cubed minus 5 x cubed\"><mn>11</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>.&nbsp;</p>","origin":"manifold","stem":"<p>Which expression is equivalent to <math alttext=\"11 x cubed minus 5 x cubed\"><mrow><mn>11</mn></mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>?</p>","externalid":"5d93e88d-9666-4e29-baab-4dcd15423597","templateid":"6514e7ba-f203-4c22-ae63-0adeac6377da","vaultid":"a9047e63-df4c-4f7e-93b3-730d39716027","type":"mcq","answerOptions":[{"id":"831050ee-a415-431c-98ee-76e5e8c5df9c","content":"<p><math alttext=\"16 x cubed\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>16</mn>\n\t<msup>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t</msup>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"f35cece2-b58c-4938-9d9a-25b5bb3b215c","content":"<p><math alttext=\"6 x cubed\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>6</mn>\n\t<msup>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t</msup>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"09555497-f9d0-4bda-80dc-62761fc4e678","content":"<p><math alttext=\"6 x Superscript 6\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>6</mn>\n\t<msup>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t<mn>6</mn>\n\t</msup>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"ca337bbe-8970-427e-a5cb-c96146b8e68f","content":"<p><math alttext=\"16 x Superscript 6\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>16</mn>\n\t<msup>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t<mn>6</mn>\n\t</msup>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"}],"correct_answer":["B"]},"createDate":1691007959822,"updateDate":1691007959822}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959822, 1691007959822),
    ($SATQ$70753f99$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$08364-DC$SATQ$, $SATQ$disclosed$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Advanced Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$P$SATQ$, $SATQ$P.C.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Nonlinear functions$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 6, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p class="stem_paragraph ">The function <span class="italic">f</span> is defined by <span class="math_expression "><span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/70753f99/img_004_0e1a13bb.png" alt="f of x equals, open parenthesis, x plus 3, close parenthesis, times, open parenthesis, x plus 1, close parenthesis"></span></span>. The graph of <span class="italic">f</span> in the <span class="italic ">xy</span>-plane is a parabola. Which of the following intervals contains the <span class="italic ">x</span>-coordinate of the vertex of the graph of <span class="italic">f</span> ?</p>
$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"a","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/70753f99/img_000_79ef75f9.png\" alt=\"negative 4 is less than x, which is less than negative 3\"></span></span></p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/70753f99/img_001_8b4f1640.png\" alt=\"negative 3 is less than x, which is less than 1\"></span></span></p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/70753f99/img_002_1f73952a.png\" alt=\"1 is less than x, which is less than 3\"></span></span></p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/70753f99/img_003_44344dfa.png\" alt=\"3 is less than x, which is less than 4\"></span></span></p>\n"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Choice B is correct. The graph of a quadratic function in the <span class="italic">xy</span>-plane is a parabola. The axis of symmetry of the parabola passes through the vertex of the parabola. Therefore, the vertex of the parabola and the midpoint of the segment between the two <span class="italic">x</span>-intercepts of the graph have the same <span class="italic">x</span>-coordinate. Since <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/70753f99/img_005_50663fa4.png" alt="f of negative 3, equals, f of negative 1, which equals 0"></span>, the <span class="italic">x</span>-coordinate of the vertex is <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/70753f99/img_006_592bf895.png" alt="the fraction with numerator negative 3 plus negative 1, and denominator 2, equals negative 2"></span>. Of the shown intervals, only the interval in choice B contains &ndash;2. Choices A, C, and D are incorrect and may result from either calculation errors or misidentification of the graph&rsquo;s <span class="italic">x</span>-intercepts.</p>
